HST Office: Save As keeps macros: it proposes a format that holds them and warns before one that does not.

New documents save as .docx, .xlsx and .pptx by default, which hold no macros, so a document with
macros lost them with no question. As in Word and Excel, Save As now proposes a format that keeps
them, and choosing or already having a format that does not asks first (Save without Macros /
Choose Another Format; the safe answer is the default). The question also covers Ctrl+S on an open
.docx and a Save As with the file named.
What a format keeps decides what is proposed: VBA projects go to .docm and .xlsm; plain Basic to
ODF, because VBA formats write only the VBA project; macros in HST Slides to .odp, because .pptm and
.ppt only copy a project read from a file (they are proposed for such a file). API saves, hidden
documents and headless runs are not affected.

